      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\), given that \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\) and \\(AB\\) is a diameter of the circle centered at \\(O\\).\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. **Identify Key Properties of the Circle:**\n   - Since \\(AB\\) is a diameter, \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\) (angle in a semicircle).\n   - \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\), so \\(\\angle ABE = 90^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 47^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Determine \\(\\angle EAD\\):**\n   - Since \\(AE\\) is a tangent at \\(E\\), \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\).\n   - \\(\\angle AEB = \\angle BAE + \\angle EAD\\).\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle EAD = 90^\\circ - \\angle BAE = 90^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 47^\\circ\\).\n\n3. **Determine \\(\\angle CED\\):**\n   - \\(\\angle CED\\) is an angle formed by the intersection of the tangents at \\(B\\) and \\(E\\) with the line \\(AE\\).\n   - The angle between two tangents from a point to a circle is equal to the angle subtended by the chord connecting the points of contact at the center.\n   - The chord \\(BE\\) subtends angle \\(\\angle BOE\\) at the center \\(O\\).\n   - Since \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle ABE = 47^\\circ\\), we can find \\(\\angle BOE\\):\n     \\[\n     \\angle BOE = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAE - \\angle ABE = 180^\\circ - 43^\\circ - 47^\\circ = 90^\\circ.\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle CED = \\frac{1}{2} \\angle BOE = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 90^\\circ = 45^\\circ\\).\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\) is \\(\\boxed{45}\\).",
